{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:11:45.659773Z","id":"b635ad3c76b6e3b4f38795df5a8893aa445dc49bbf21f0332974e2e6bfbe65eb","body":{"detail":"The check is called as parent_id_graph(&view_first, &view_second) (line 1020): both views come out of harness B's reader, so it tests B's idempotence, not that A's linkage survived export. It also walks a turn's parent through any event id before comparing. Exporting the Claude and Codex fixtures to Pi currently gives 7 of 67 and 5 of 10 entries with a parentId that names no entry in the projected session, and the matrix stays green.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":797},"end":{"line":836},"content_hash":"44325fed4f288d76ae47cbaa356cd9608d07331dc43f1a116b9f2a7406658714"},"suggested_fix":"Add a per-harness check that every parent link in the projected native session names an entry in that session (for harnesses that write parents: Claude, Pi), and compare the source view's turn graph against view_first, not only view_first against view_second.","summary":"parent_id_graph compares only two passes through the same target harness and resolves parents past events, so a projector that writes parents naming entries it dropped still passes","tags":["review","review:pr-144-qual-3","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:16:20.346222Z","id":"b4573c9b304eb93645e569f65150437d026fdef3f919d7444938ac76081727c1","body":{"detail":"crates/path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs:1020 calls parent_id_graph(&view_first, &view_second); lines 807-823 resolve a turn's parent through any event id (the event-skipping is new in this diff; main compared raw (id, parent_id)). A throwaway test running test-fixtures/claude/convo.jsonl and test-fixtures/codex/convo.jsonl through to_view + PiProjector found 7 of 66 and 5 of 9 non-header entries with a parentId naming no entry; `cargo test -p path-cli --test cross_harness_matrix` still passes (matrix_translation ok, matrix_schema_validation ok).","kind":"comment","references":"b635ad3c76b6e3b4f38795df5a8893aa445dc49bbf21f0332974e2e6bfbe65eb","summary":"confirmed: regression in test coverage - parent_id_graph only compares two passes through the target harness and now skips past events, so the Claude->Pi and Codex->Pi dangling parents pass the matrix","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T20:47:24.917656Z","id":"612cdc4cb8aa05c3680161c61739a19735d1066288336d25b37f95ba25f99637","body":{"detail":"Owner approval, 2026-10-13 (after reading the list). In scope for #144: the PR keeps Claude and Codex derivations prefix-stable and naturally ordered; the event-chain model stays (78dd6c89) and the translations are made to work under it. Part of the #144 fix pass.","kind":"decision","references":"b635ad3c76b6e3b4f38795df5a8893aa445dc49bbf21f0332974e2e6bfbe65eb","suggested_fix":"Add a per-harness check that every parent link in the projected native session names an entry in that session (for harnesses that write parents: Claude, Pi), and compare the source view's turn graph against view_first, not only view_first against view_second.","summary":"Decided: fix; the cross-harness matrix asserts no dangling parent after the first translation leg","tags":["review:pr-144-qual-3","decision","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/tests/cross_harness_matrix.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T21:04:24.873732Z","id":"ab91ff5de49548f66ec935259defc15f98c6bb3ff3b068031ff2582177ca571a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:56da06a","summary":"Fixed in 56da06a on ben/items-ir: each matrix cell checks that every parent the Claude and Pi projectors write on the first leg names an entry of the written session (Claude: an entry of a Claude Code type). Evidence: cargo test -p path-cli --test cross_harness_matrix passes; against the pre-fix projectors it flags claude->pi, codex->pi, codex->claude, gemini->claude and gemini->pi. The source-vs-view_first turn-graph comparison from the suggested fix was not added.","supersedes":"b635ad3c76b6e3b4f38795df5a8893aa445dc49bbf21f0332974e2e6bfbe65eb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
